WEBVTT

00:38:55.384 --> 00:39:00.271
Because they can
intellectually understand,

00:39:00.295 --> 00:39:02.695
but I don't think they really feel it.

00:39:02.719 --> 00:39:04.310
AG: Yeah, so that would be,

00:39:04.334 --> 00:39:06.290
well in some language cognitive empathy,

00:39:06.314 --> 00:39:08.118
but not emotional empathy.

00:39:08.142 --> 00:39:09.310
DF: Right.

00:39:09.334 --> 00:39:10.556
AG: Very interesting.

00:39:10.580 --> 00:39:12.087
They can take your perspective,

00:39:12.111 --> 00:39:13.586
they know what you're feeling,

00:39:13.610 --> 00:39:15.675
and that makes it very easy
to get you to do

00:39:15.699 --> 00:39:16.929
what they want you to do.

00:39:16.953 --> 00:39:18.117
DF: Yeah.

00:39:18.141 --> 00:39:20.150
AG: Let me ask you this then,

00:39:20.174 --> 00:39:23.871
when this all came
crashing down during the IPO,

00:39:23.895 --> 00:39:25.878
what was your emotional reaction?

00:39:28.157 --> 00:39:29.507
DF: I was really sad.